  "reason": "Evidence: config_036 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) achieved the best validation accuracy (0.715) and F1 (0.687), substantially outperforming both RNA-only (0.650) and the resnet50-based multimodal (0.632). This establishes that the combination of scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile + avgpool is the strongest design. Uncertainty: The only untested dimension within this top-performing configuration is the fusion strategy (concat vs. weighted). Question tested: Does weighted fusion improve over simple concatenation when combining the scvi_n200 RNA embedding with the imagenet_vit_l image embedding? Why this is the best next experiment: It is a minimal, single-variable change from the current best configuration, so any performance delta is cleanly attributable to the fusion method. If weighted fusion helps, we immediately identify an even better configuration; if not, we confirm concat is optimal and can redirect exploration. Under a limited budget, exploiting the strongest direction with the smallest remaining uncertainty is the most efficient use of the next experiment."
}

